me page: <math alttext=\"left parenthesis 40 right parenthesis left parenthesis StartFraction 190 Over 100 EndFraction right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mn>40</mn></mfenced><mfenced><mfrac><mn>190</mn><mn>100</mn></mfrac></mfenced></math>, or <math alttext=\"76\"><mn>76</mn>\n</math> comments. Thus, the estimated number of comments for the following hour is the sum of the comments from the end of the previous hour and the number of additional comments, which is <math alttext=\"40 plus 76\"><mn>40</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>76</mn></math>, or <math alttext=\"116\"><mn>116</mn>\n</math>. This means that when <math alttext=\"t equals 1\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>t</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>1</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"upper C equals 116\"><mrow>\n\t<mi>C</mi>\n\t<mo>=</mo>\n\t<mn>116</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"1\"><mn>1</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"t\"><mi>t</mi>\n</math>, <math alttext=\"116\"><mn>116</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"upper C\"><mi>C</mi>\n</math>, and <math alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"upper K\"><mi>K</mi>\n</math> in the equation <math alttext=\"upper C equals upper K a Superscript t\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></math> yields <math alttext=\"116 equals 40 a Superscript 1\"><mn>116</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>1</mn></msup></math>, or <math alttext=\"116 equals 40 a\"><mn>116</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>40</mn><mi>a</mi></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn>\n</math> yields <math alttext=\"2.9 equals a\"><mn>2.9</mn><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi></math>. Substituting <math alttext=\"40\"><mn>40</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"upper K\"><mi>K</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"2.9\"><mn>2.9</mn>\n</math> for <math alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi>\n</math> in the equation <math alttext=\"upper C equals upper K a Superscript t\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>K</mi><msup><mi>a</mi><mi>t</mi></msup></math> yields <math alttext=\"upper C equals 40 