</math>, the maximum or minimum value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math> occurs at the value of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> halfway between any two values of <math alttext="x"><mi>x</mi>
</math> that have the same corresponding value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
</math>. The table shows that <em>x</em>-values of <math alttext="21"><mn>21</mn>
</math> and <math alttext="25"><mn>25</mn>
</math> correspond to the same <em>y</em>-value, <math alttext="negative 8"><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></math>. Since <math alttext="23"><mn>23</mn>
</math> is halfway between <math alttext="21"><mn>21</mn>
</math> and <math alttext="25"><mn>25</mn>
</math>, the maximum or minimum value of <math alttext="y"><mi>y</mi>
