<p style="text-align: left;">What is the positive solution to the given equation?</p>$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$["9"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["9"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">The correct answer is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="9"><mn>9</mn></math>. Dividing both sides of the given equation by <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="5"><mn>5</mn></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartAbsoluteValue x EndAbsoluteValue equals 9"><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>. By the definition of absolute value, if <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="StartAbsoluteValue x EndAbsoluteValue equals 9"><mo>|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>|</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>, then <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x equals 9"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math> or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x equals negative 9"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></math>. Therefore, the two solutions to the equation <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="5 StartAbsoluteValue x EndAbsoluteValue equals 45"><mn>5</mn><mfenced open="|" close="|"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn></math> are <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="9"><mn>9</mn></math> and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="negative 9"><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></math>.&nbsp;It follows that the positive solution to the given equation is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="9"><mn>9</mn></math>.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"13e5a5d5","external_id":"711ce341-6b08-4443-a2bc-e3ddb891f609","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"46235812-e2ba-4e78-a6b3-4fa8266ca1b1","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.B.","skill_desc":"Non