egative 9\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></math>. Therefore, the two solutions to the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"5 StartAbsoluteValue x EndAbsoluteValue equals 45\"><mn>5</mn><mfenced open=\"|\" close=\"|\"><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>45</mn></math> are <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 9\"><mo>-</mo><mn>9</mn></math>.&nbsp;It follows that the positive solution to the given equation is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"9\"><mn>9</mn></math>.</p>","externalid":"711ce341-6b08-4443-a2bc-e3ddb891f609","correct_answer":["9"]},"createDate":1755117017719,"updateDate":1755117017719}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017719, 1755117017719),
    ($SATQ$158591f0$SATQ$, $SATQ$30e5c8c1-d494-443c-a28f-3d8867feefed$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.B.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Nonlinear equations in one variable and systems of equations in two variables $SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, 6, $SATQ$spr$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: center;"><math alttext="x left parenthesis x plus 1 right parenthesis minus 56 equals 4 x left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis"><mrow>
