</math> is defined by the given equation. Which of the following equivalent forms of the equation displays the maximum value of the function as a constant or coefficient?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"170b8aef-e897-4486-8cea-0af2122ade3a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals minus 6 x squared plus 42 x plus 18 x minus 126\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>42</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>126</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"44eec19a-39c4-4ced-b5ea-25f0074c6a73","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals minus 6 x left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis plus 18 left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"42d6fb0f-30e2-467d-8442-2d042138f90c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals minus 6 left parenthesis x minus 5 right parenthesis squared plus 24\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>24</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"90c13897-b39a-40ac-9a7a-5a76e8276f26","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals minus 6 left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis x minus 3 right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t<mfenced>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t</mfenced>\n\t<mfenced>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t</mfenced>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["C"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["42d6fb0f-30e2-467d-8442-2d042138f90c"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is correct. The given equation is quadratic. The maximum value of a function defined by a quadratic equation can be displayed as a constant in the vertex form of the equation, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus k"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></math>, where the maximum value of the function is <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="k"><mi>k</mi></math>, which occurs when <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x equals h"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></math>, and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a"><mi>a</mi></math> is a constant. The given equation can be rewritten in this form by completing the square. To complete the square, the given equation can be rewritten as <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals minus 6 left parenthesis x squared minus 10 x right parenthesis minus 126"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>126</mn></math>, which is equivalent to <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals minus 6 left parenthesis x squared minus 10 x plus 25 right parenthesis minus 126 plus 6 left parenthesis 25 right parenthesis"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>126</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals minus 6 left parenthesis x minus 5 right parenthesis squared plus 24"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>24</mn></math>. This equation is in vertex form, where <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="a equals negative 6"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math>, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="h equals 5"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>, and <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="k equals 24"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></math>. Therefore, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals minus 6 left parenthesis x minus 5 right parenthesis squared plus 24"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>24</mn></math> displays the maximum value, <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="24"><mn>24</mn></math>, of the function as a constant.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect. This form displays one of the zeros, not the maximum value, of the function as a constant.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect. This form displays the zeros, not the maximum value, of the function as constants.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"16aa9758","external_id":"37d40ac0-74f9-4d4a-8168-1a7d28a874f2","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"900f3a4e-1d37-48c3-a1d8-64412fea1bc7","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.C.","skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","difficulty":"H","score_band_range_cd":6,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals minus 6 x squared plus 60 x minus 126\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>60</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mn>126</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> is defined by the given equation. Which of the following equivalent forms of the equation displays the maximum value of the function as a constant or coefficient?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"170b8aef-e897-4486-8cea-0af2122ade3a","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals minus 6 x squared plus 42 x plus 18 x minus 126\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>42</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>126</mn></math></p>"},{"id":"44eec19a-39c4-4ced-b5ea-25f0074c6a73","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals minus 6 x left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis plus 18 left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><mn>18</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>)</mo></math></p>"},{"id":"42d6fb0f-30e2-467d-8442-2d042138f90c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals minus 6 left parenthesis x minus 5 right parenthesis squared plus 24\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mfenced>\n\t\t\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t\t\t<mn>5</mn>\n\t\t\t\t</mrow>\n\t\t\t</mfenced>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mn>24</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"90c13897-b39a-40ac-9a7a-5a76e8276f26","content":"<p><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals minus 6 left parenthesis x minus 7 right parenthesis left parenthesis x minus 3 right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t<mfenced>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t<mn>7</mn>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t</mfenced>\n\t<mfenced>\n\t\t<mrow>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t\t<mn>3</mn>\n\t\t</mrow>\n\t</mfenced>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["42d6fb0f-30e2-467d-8442-2d042138f90c"],"correct_answer":["C"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice C is correct. The given equation is quadratic. The maximum value of a function defined by a quadratic equation can be displayed as a constant in the vertex form of the equation, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals a left parenthesis x minus h right parenthesis squared plus k\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>h</mi><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mi>k</mi></math>, where the maximum value of the function is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k\"><mi>k</mi></math>, which occurs when <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x equals h\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>h</mi></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a\"><mi>a</mi></math> is a constant. The given equation can be rewritten in this form by completing the square. To complete the square, the given equation can be rewritten as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals minus 6 left parenthesis x squared minus 10 x right parenthesis minus 126\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>126</mn></math>, which is equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals minus 6 left parenthesis x squared minus 10 x plus 25 right parenthesis minus 126 plus 6 left parenthesis 25 right parenthesis\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>(</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>10</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>126</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>25</mn><mo>)</mo></math>, or <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals minus 6 left parenthesis x minus 5 right parenthesis squared plus 24\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>24</mn></math>. This equation is in vertex form, where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"a equals negative 6\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></math>, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"h equals 5\"><mi>h</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math>, and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"k equals 24\"><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>24</mn></math>. Therefore, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals minus 6 left parenthesis x minus 5 right parenthesis squared plus 24\"><mi>f</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>24</mn></math> displays the maximum value, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"24\"><mn>24</mn></math>, of the function as a constant.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice B is incorrect. This form displays one of the zeros, not the maximum value, of the function as a constant.</p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice D is incorrect. This form displays the zeros, not the maximum value, of the function as constants.</p>","parenttemplatename":null,"parenttemplateid":null,"templateclusterid":null,"templateclustername":null,"origin":null,"position":null,"image_count":0,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1776362727992,"pPcc":"SAT#P","questionId":"16aa9758","skill_cd":"P.C.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Nonlinear functions","createDate":1776362727992,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Advanced Math","ibn":"","external_id":"37d40ac0-74f9-4d4a-8168-1a7d28a874f2","primary_class_cd":"P","uId":"900f3a4e-1d37-48c3-a1d8-64412fea1bc7","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"type":"mcq","stem":"<p style=\"text-align: center;\"><math alttext=\"f left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals minus 6 x squared plus 60 x minus 126\"><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mrow>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t\t<mn>6</mn>\n\t\t<msup>\n\t\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t\t\t<mn>2</mn>\n\t\t</msup>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>+</mo>\n\t<mrow>\n\t\t<mn>60</mn>\n\t\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t</mrow>\n\t<mo>-</mo>\n\t<mn>126</mn>\n</mrow>\n</math></p>\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math> is defined by the given equ