    ($SATQ$18c7c3e0$SATQ$, $SATQ$4aae6d4f-125f-4c81-812c-7d232ae7986c$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Advanced Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$P$SATQ$, $SATQ$P.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Equivalent expressions$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Which expression is equivalent to&nbsp;<math alttext="13 x squared minus 7 x squared"><mrow><mn>13</mn></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"302ad3f0-b679-4711-be9a-44f656475017","content":"<p><math alttext=\"minus 91 x squared\"><mo>-</mo><mn>91</mn>\n<msup>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e9aa6012-cabb-4127-aedc-57840dfe9eae","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6 x squared\"><mn>6</mn>\n<msup>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"8e92c360-8b6b-4c50-a38e-3aedff55502b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"20 x squared\"><mn>20</mn>\n<msup>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"ce61ae9d-4b18-4e61-b35b-926faefdafa3","content":"<p><math alttext=\"40 x squared\"><mn>40</mn>\n<msup>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["B"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["e9aa6012-cabb-4127-aedc-57840dfe9eae"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p>Choice B is correct. Since each term in the given expression has a common factor of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x squared"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, it can be rewritten as <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 13 minus 7 right parenthesis x squared"><mo>(</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>)</mo><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, or <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="6 x squared"><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>. Therefore, the expression <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="6 x squared"><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> is equivalent to <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="13 x squared minus 7 x squared"><mn>13</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>
<p>Alternate approach: Since the two terms of the given expression are both constant multiples of <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="x squared"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, they are like terms and can, therefore, be combined through subtraction. Subtracting like terms in the expression <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="13 x squared minus 7 x squared"><mn>13</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> yields <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="6 x squared"><mn>6</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>
<p>Choice A is incorrect. This expression is equivalent to&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="left parenthesis 13 x right parenthesis left parenthesis minus 7 x right parenthesis"><mo>(</mo><mn>13</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>)</mo></math>, not&nbsp;<math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="13 x squared minus 7 x squared"><mn>13</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>
<p>Choice C is incorrect. This expression is equivalent to <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="13 x squared plus 7 x squared"><mn>13</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>7</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, not <math xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML" alttext="13 x squared minus 7 x squared"><mn>13</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>.</p>
<p>Choice D is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"18c7c3e0","external_id":"4aae6d4f-125f-4c81-812c-7d232ae7986c","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":null,"uId":"9022835c-fb5b-45a4-b57e-2013f0d93619","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"P","domain":"Advanced Math","skill_cd":"P.A.","skill_desc":"Equivalent expressions","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":2,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Which expression is equivalent to&nbsp;<math alttext=\"13 x squared minus 7 x squared\"><mrow><mn>13</mn></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mrow><mn>7</mn></mrow><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"302ad3f0-b679-4711-be9a-44f656475017","content":"<p><math alttext=\"minus 91 x squared\"><mo>-</mo><mn>91</mn>\n<msup>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"e9aa6012-cabb-4127-aedc-57840dfe9eae","content":"<p><math alttext=\"6 x squared\"><mn>6</mn>\n<msup>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"8e92c360-8b6b-4c50-a38e-3aedff55502b","content":"<p><math alttext=\"20 x squared\"><mn>20</mn>\n<msup>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"ce61ae9d-4b18-4e61-b35b-926faefdafa3","content":"<p><math alttext=\"40 x squared\"><mn>40</mn>\n<msup>\n\t<mi>x</mi>\n\t<mn>2</mn>\n</msup>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["e9aa6012-cabb-4127-aedc-57840dfe9eae"],"correct_answer":["B"],"rationale":"<p>Choice B is correct. Since each term in the given expression has a common factor of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"x squared\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>, it can be rewritten as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis 13 minus 7 right parenthesis x squared\"><mo>(</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>)</mo><msup><mi>x</mi